# Prime review — Grok replay Colab 05.02

Date: 2026-10-30. Reviewer: Codex Prime. Original return and capture 0173 unchanged.
Disposition: useful contextual Colab; two manual outputs complete and two assisted
routes explicitly partial. No reliable efficiency ratio or general model ranking.

Prime freshly verified 0173 custody and every exported artifact-index entry.
artifact-check.json records the count; all match, as do N7/N1/exported return bytes.
Measurement command counts, sums and byte totals match retained operation ends.
Prime read the proposed pack and case-B review; it did not rerun Grok's four runs.
Historical comparison is now allowed because all three submissions are preserved.

## G-01 — Packaging failure and protection: accepted
Grok confirms missing clerk_adapter.py and five missing historical benchmark
dependencies. It did not patch bindings or add files to make the first run clean.
The record refusal is protective behavior; the failure still belongs to preparation.
No fresh 32-test result was produced. Keep both assisted cycles partial.

## G-02 — Long run was not endless retry: supported by retained account
The return and operations show bounded attempts and subsequent review work rather
than repeated unchanged repairs. Do not infer inability from the Director's elapsed
25-minute observation. Actual elapsed summaries end at clock probes before some
writing; they are not equivalent to other models' timing boundaries.

Prime sent a checkpoint prompt through the Director during Grok's run. That prompt
asked for status, stopped unchanged retries and permitted honest partial completion;
it supplied no expected subject finding. Preserve it as a method intervention even
though Grok's own interventions fields discuss only technical steps. Do not rewrite
its sealed measurements or claim an intervention-free comparison.

## G-03 — Status versus completeness: preserve the distinctions
Case A: Grok accepts the initial pass while keeping the broader goal open and
proposing later controls. Codex called the unfinished integration correction-required;
these are different pass boundaries, not equivalent outcome labels. Historical
review accepted the first foundation and held actual comparison for correction.
Case B: Grok/Claude complete the bounded helper goal; Codex left broader integration
open. A comparison must bind the stated goal before grading completion.

## G-04 — Safe treatment of unavailable history: accepted
Grok did not run old specimen requests into the live work book, and distinguished
recorded historical/live classifications from fresh verification. Missing objects
in a disposable Git repository are not proof the original Builder lost them.
Do not rerun retained instructions as active commands.

## G-05 — Nested evidence gap: missed, already independently resolved
Grok and Codex top-level audits missed Claude's nested specimen-file omission.
The actual original Git/local files all exist and match; the first replay selection
omitted 19 files. Preserve Claude's additional finding and this miss, rather than
calling all three reviews identical. No packet-helper rebuild follows.

## G-06 — Journal cutoff and exit layers: incorporate into repair
Some day reads overlapped in-flight operations. Their counts describe their read
cut, not an eventual total. A final evidence export should either wait for all
declared run operations or state its cutoff/incomplete observations. Do not rewrite
prior snapshots until they look tidy. Preserve child exit, wrapper/shell exit if
exposed, and which layer is being counted; external shell status may differ.

## G-07 — Historical proposal is not a current work order
The old benchmark's proposed controls broadly agree with the historical repair.
That repair was already accepted in 0166, with 31 revised tests and the delivered-
input drift probe. Do not release Grok's historical next-pack against today's
instrument or reopen completed work merely because a replay proposed it.
Compare wording/commitments and cost coverage carefully; no automatic grading by
agreement with old prose. Keep reported versus independently checked results distinct.

## Next action
Finalize the preparation and adapter drafts from the combined dispositions, retain
all original evidence, then execute only explicitly released bounded repair slices.
No need for a larger kernel redesign or a second experiment before these faults
are fixed. AR-01 remains held. No source code change made by this review.
